<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kannur</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Cannanore</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kannur, formerly Cannanore, is a city on the Malabar coast of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kerala">Kerala</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. A port of the spice trade, it was linked with the Kolathiri rulers and was the seat of the Arakkal family, the only Muslim royal house of Kerala. The Portuguese built <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/st-angelo-fort">St Angelo Fort</a> there in 1505, later held by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> and the British.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kannur.jpg" alt="Kannur" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kidu (talk) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kannur_Skyline_3.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
